      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T23:03:27Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): part-in-spindle mode and table tool stations on a mill\n\nA mill setup can hold the part in its spindle (a collet) with lathe tools\non the table. SetupDef::part_in_spindle states the stock's length offset\nregister, the collet stick-out and outer diameter, and the table\nstations: each tool's own 1-based work offset, approach side (-X/+X) and\nspindle direction (M3/M4). Two tools never share one work offset.\n\nThe undoable SetPartInSpindle and SetTableStation commands and the MCP\ntools set_part_in_spindle and set_table_station configure it; get_job\nshows it; the project file keeps it as an additive key, and the loader\nrefuses a record the commands would refuse.\n\nIn the mode, the family door admits turning work and an axial Drill and\nrefuses milling and cross holes by name; the setup's work is generated\nas a lathe's (the axial door and the spindle law hold), and the lathe\nfield eye simulates it. The collet's workholding max rpm is required and\nenforced; with no post section for table stations yet, the post is\nrefused by name.\n\nFixes #3406\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
